KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --object-bits 12 --stdlib libc++ --unwind 12 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ no read error: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ failed: 0, a limit, or nothing extracted: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
libc++: locale::use_facet is defined in libc++'s compiled library and
has no model, so get() dereferences a nondeterministic __shared_count
and cin.fail() always holds (the WRONG assertion holds).  The same
gap as cpp11_ostream_integer_insertion_libcxx.
